# Buildroot users table (makeusers): groups the image defines.
# seat: seatd.service runs `seatd -g seat`; members may open the seat, i.e. run
# the COSMIC compositor as themselves. The installer adds the desktop user.
- -1 seat -1 - - - - -
# bluetooth: BlueZ's D-Bus policy grants the bluetooth group access to bluetoothd.
- -1 bluetooth -1 - - - - -
# input: systemd's 50-udev-default.rules gives every /dev/input device to this
# group at mode 0660, and the image has no systemd-sysusers to create it — so
# `input` existed only as the cosmic-greeter's supplementary group, and a
# desktop user could not read a game controller. The installer adds the owner
# (USER_GROUPS lists input) and merge-accounts adds existing owners once.
- -1 input -1 - - - - -
# cosmic-greeter: the login screen runs as this system user (greetd's
# default_session). Locked password; the seat and GPU/input device groups let
# its cosmic-comp open the display.
cosmic-greeter -1 cosmic-greeter -1 ! /var/lib/cosmic-greeter /bin/false seat,video,render,input COSMIC login screen
# fwupd-refresh: fwupd-refresh.service (enabled by its timer) runs
# `fwupdmgr refresh` as this user. Upstream creates it with a sysusers.d entry;
# the image has no systemd-sysusers, so without this row the unit died with
# 217/USER every time the timer fired.
fwupd-refresh -1 fwupd-refresh -1 * - - - fwupd metadata refresh
# gamemode: GameMode's polkit rule grants the governor/GPU-clock helpers to this
# group only (allow_active=no for everyone else) and limits.d gives it a nice
# limit. Upstream creates it with sysusers.d, which the image never runs: GameMode
# changed nothing on any machine. The installer adds the desktop user
# (USER_GROUPS), merge-accounts adds existing owners once.
- -1 gamemode -1 - - - - -
# power: thermald's D-Bus policy names it; dbus-daemon logged 'Unknown group
# "power"' at every boot.
- -1 power -1 - - - - -
